# Claude Code local state
.claude/settings.local.json

# Consumer-shaped artifacts written by hooks and fixtures run against this repo.
# The hooks take CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR and will happily write a pipeline flow log,
# a snapshot or a sensor sidecar into the distribution root when a fixture or a
# manual guard invocation points them here. Nothing consumed them, but a broad
# `git add -A` committed one in v0.126.0 -- the same way the budget validator's
# scan channels used to get committed before they moved to mktemp.
_bmad-output/

# `.claude/` is excluded as its CONTENTS (`.claude/*`), not as the directory
# (`.claude/`), and that distinction is the whole of this block. Git does not
# descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so with `.claude/` no negation beneath it can
# ever re-include anything -- the negations parse, apply to nothing, and the file
# stays ignored while the .gitignore reads as though it were tracked. Measured: the
# first attempt here used `.claude/` plus two negations and `git check-ignore` still
# reported `.claude/rules/a.md` IGNORED.
#
# The exception is the authoring rulebook. `.claude/rules/**/*.md` is exactly what
# Claude Code's own loader reads -- recursively, `.md` only -- so the trackable set
# and the loaded set are one set by construction. Every other path under `.claude/`
# stays ignored, which is what preserves the property the comment above protects:
# anything a hook writes here that is not a rule file cannot be committed.
# Bound mechanically by the tracked-path assertion in `.githooks/pre-push`.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
.claude/rules/**
!.claude/rules/**/
!.claude/rules/**/*.md
